# CAMPAIGN STATE IS NOT SOURCE. Everything in discovery_okuda/campaign/ except the four inputs
# below is written by a running loop and DELETED by campaign_loop.clean_start() at every launch --
# so committing it buys nothing and costs the one thing that actually hurt: `git stash` and
# `git restore` will happily rewrite a live campaign's registry underneath the process using it.
# That happened twice on 4 August. The second time, a stash taken while a campaign was running
# rolled hypotheses.jsonl back to a dead campaign's copy; round 2 then posed a hypothesis id that
# copy already held and died with `R2.0.f4907e already posed`, and the live round's own records
# went with the dropped stash.
#
# The research record is elsewhere and stays tracked: discovery_okuda/_archive/, the _failed_*
# snapshots, and the note. What is kept here is only what a fresh clone NEEDS to run a campaign --
# the two templates, the standing instructions, and the human's channel -- which are exactly the
# files clean_start() preserves by name.
discovery_okuda/campaign/*
!discovery_okuda/campaign/TEMPLATE_analysis.md
!discovery_okuda/campaign/TEMPLATE_memory.md
!discovery_okuda/campaign/instruction.md
!discovery_okuda/campaign/user_input.md

# ECM sweep output: movies and strips, regenerated by prototype/ecm/sweep.py
log/okuda_ECM/
